   "text": {
    "L1": "We will share 96 rupees equally among 4 children.",
    "L2": "Share the tens first. Nine tens gives each child two tens, with one ten left.",
    "L3": "Change the leftover ten into ten ones. Ten plus six makes sixteen ones.",
    "L4": "Share sixteen ones among four children. Each child gets four ones.",
    "L5": "So each child gets two tens and four ones: 24 rupees.",
    "L6": "Check by multiplying back: four times 24 equals 96.",
    "L7": "Do not divide each digit separately. The leftover ten must join the ones."
   },
